package assignment.piece;

import assignment.protocol.Game;
import assignment.protocol.Move;
import assignment.protocol.Piece;
import assignment.protocol.Place;
import assignment.protocol.Player;

/**
 * Global rule that requires that a piece should not go to a destination where there is another piece belonging to the
 * same player.
 */
public class OccupiedRule implements Rule {
    @Override
    public boolean validate(Game game, Move move) {
        Piece sourcePiece = game.getPiece(move.getSource());
        Piece destinationPiece = game.getPiece(move.getDestination());

        // If there's no piece at destination, move is valid
        if (destinationPiece == null) {
            return true;
        }

        // Move is valid only if destination piece belongs to different player
        return !sourcePiece.getPlayer().equals(destinationPiece.getPlayer());
    }

    @Override
    public String getDescription() {
        return "piece cannot be captured by another piece belonging to the same player";
    }
}
```

This implementation:

1. Gets the piece at the source position using `game.getPiece(move.getSource())`
2. Gets the piece at the destination position using `game.getPiece(move.getDestination())`
3. If there's no piece at the destination (null), the move is automatically valid
4. If there is a piece at the destination, checks if it belongs to the same player as the moving piece
5. Returns true (valid move) only if the destination piece belongs to a different player or is empty
6. Returns false (invalid move) if the destination piece belongs to the same player

The rule follows the description that a piece cannot move to a position occupied by another piece of the same player, which is a common rule in many board games to prevent friendly captures.

