   - Less than the board size (upper bound, since board coordinates are 0-indexed)
4. Returns true only if both source and destination are within bounds
5. Returns false if either place is out of bounds

The helper method makes the code more readable and avoids duplication of the bounds checking logic.

The rule follows the principle that any move that tries to go outside the board boundaries should be considered invalid, which is a fundamental rule for most board games.

